        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "Executive Order 6954 (January 31, 1935) is a approval of an amendment to the Code of Fair Competition for the Distilled Spirits Rectifying Industry and modification of the earlier approval to cover the code as amended under section 3 of Title I of the National Industrial Recovery Act. Read in full from the held American Presidency Project transcription (page record checked; identity, date and subject confirmed against the census register and the WPA 1944 list); the order's own text states no limit on the approval. Its command depends entirely on the code approval, so its first end is the repeal of the code-approval and code-enforcement provisions of Title I by section 2 of S.J. Res. 113 on June 14, 1935, applying SHARED_ANALYSIS.md and its adjudication; Schechter (May 27, 1935) is recorded as a validity characterization only.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"The order states no period, \\\"until\\\" date, condition or provisional approval that limits the approval, and no stay or postponement to a fixed date. Held orders naming the code before this order are EO 6487-B, 6685, 6812 and 6945; after it, EO 7017 (April 19, 1935) and EO 7022 (April 20, 1935). I read the operative sentence of each: each approves amendments and modifies the previous approval to include an approval of the code in its entirety as amended. None cancels, suspends, supersedes or revokes the approval, so the later orders are later events. No held text cites this order by number. No held record shows this code cancelled, suspended, superseded or revoked before June 14, 1935, and none shows a modification under section 10(b) that reached this order's command. June 16, 1935 is not an end, because section 1 of S.J. Res. 113 replaced that expiry with April 1, 1936. Schechter (May 27, 1935) is a validity characterization, not an end date.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"No appointment, delegation, direction to a government agency, report direction or other command independent of the code approval appears. The \\\"Approval recommended\\\" and signature lines command nothing.\",\"savings_check\":\"Read S.J. Res. 113 section 2 and its proviso and NIRA section 5 in the packet excerpts. No held source continues this approval, a prosecution under it or any command of this order after June 14, 1935; accrued acts, liabilities and the section 5 exemption for completed action are recorded as transferred or accrued and not as continued operation.\",\"scope_check\":\"One operative command: the approval stated in the quoted sentence. The recitals (application, hearings, the Administrator's report and findings) command nothing, and the order reproduces no code text, which is not needed because the approval is the only source of the code's legal effect. The single machine clause covers the whole command.\"}",
